        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/e480ec/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-20T16:29:42.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"brytehfryguy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/f0a364/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> brytehfryguy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>BlueHairedMeerkat wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Not quite. H is minimum 3, but so is the number of heroes. If you're playing with two heroes, there's no reason not to set H=2, since what you're doing is unsupported by the rules either way.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nA lot of villains don't even function at H=2 so if you want to  play  at 2, it is strongly suggested to make H=3 so the game is playable. Chris has even supported this idea, iirc.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I know the game isn't balanced for only 2 heroes. &nbsp;Neither is it balanced for 5+ heroes. &nbsp;But it does work. &nbsp;Do H-2 effects get stopped with only 2 heroes, yes. &nbsp;But I assure you, this is a good thing. &nbsp;Sure, for some two-heroes match-ups it makes the villan a push-over. &nbsp;But it makes it so any two-hero match-up is viable. &nbsp;And no villian is completely stopped with H=2.</p>\n<p>And again, feel free to play how you like. &nbsp;I'm just providing my experiences in H=2 and H=5+ games.</p>",
        "post_number": 29,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:17:06.325Z",
